MODIFICATIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

In accordance with Apache License 2.0, section 4(b) — "You must cause any
modified files to carry prominent notices stating that You changed the
files" — notice is given that the files in this repository have been
substantially changed from the upstream work. Principal modifications:

  * Product renamed from whisperASR to SonicScribe (声记); user-facing
    branding, bundle identifier and URL scheme changed (the legacy
    `whisperasr://` scheme is still accepted). Internal identifiers — the
    Swift package name, the Application Support directory and the log
    directory — were deliberately left as `WhisperASR` so that existing
    user history and downloaded models need no migration.

  * Multi-engine ASR layer: Apple SpeechAnalyzer, Qwen3-ASR (GGUF/Metal),
    NVIDIA Nemotron (Core ML / ANE), FunASR (SenseVoice-Small and
    Paraformer via sherpa-onnx), online cloud APIs and a remote-LAN
    provider, behind a single dispatching service with watchdog and
    automatic degradation.

  * Audio front end: Silero neural VAD combined with zero-crossing-rate
    and energy filtering, adaptive noise-floor estimation, and O(1)
    amortised buffer compaction.

  * Subtitle and translation: unified floating capsule overlay, bilingual
    dual-layer rendering with typewriter streaming, OBS / Cleanfeed
    chroma-key output window, translation pipeline with prompt templates,
    streaming SSE client and key-free public translation channels.

  * Local OpenAI-compatible HTTP API server (transcriptions, translations,
    model listing).

  * AI meeting-minutes service, interactive timestamped transcript
    playback, and SRT / VTT / Markdown / TXT / JSON export.

  * Settings reorganised into seven sub-modules.

  * Added local benchmark and evaluation tooling: Scripts/sonic_asr_mcp.py
    (an MCP server exposing the on-device engines) and a companion ASR
    workbench, plus the whisper-cli based speech-translation path.

  * Removed the upstream Traditional Chinese README (README.zh-TW.md) and
    replaced the documentation set with README.md / README.zh-cn.md and
    the files under docs/.


